I need proper handling: create a fresh regex per call, or don't reset. Since REQUIRE_RE is module-level and shared, concurrent/sequential calls with /g state is the classic bug. Correct approach: reset lastIndex only when starting, and DON'T reset between execs:

```js
function requireSpecs(source) {
    var specs = [];
    var re = new RegExp(REQUIRE_RE.source, 'g'); // fresh stateful copy per call
    var m = re.exec(source);
    while (m !== null) {
        specs.push(m[2]);
        m = re.exec(source);
    }
    return specs;
}
```

