```

But then `const zip = buildPack(agent, next);` doesn't literally exist → test still fails. Hmm. The test hard-codes implementation details of main. The test is a GUARD (gh-690/launch-contract era) — its intent is ordering. I shouldn't weaken a guard test to fit my implementation... but the assertion is legitimately about "augment between compile and validation". My refactor keeps that ordering — the guard test's LETTER breaks.

